# kill-thesis verdict ledger — one line per verdict, appended by the skill.
# Format: <YYYY-MM-DD> <TICKER or slug> <VERDICT> conditions=<n> refuted=<n> unknown=<n> [reopen=<YYYY-MM-DD|event>:<slug>]
# Purpose: makes verdict drift measurable (see the design note in
# .claude/skills/kill-thesis/SKILL.md — the one-way-check freeze is revisited
# at ten verdicts). Nothing in sources/ reads this file.
# reopen= is the thesis's stated revisit trigger; the slug is a pointer, the
# thesis file is the source of truth. Dated reopens are surfaced by the
# nightly ntfy (deploy/launchd/daily_summary.py) when due; the dashboard's
# research-reopens section lists every open trigger, event: ones included.
# Only a ticker's newest line counts -- a re-research retires the old trigger.
# Absent reopen= means the thesis states no reopen condition. Backfilled
# 2026-07-29 from each thesis's falsifier/verdict prose.
